course: dictionary
lesson: 6426
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, tells you which meaning the writer wants. Muzzle is a good example, so read the clues before you choose.
explain: «Kieran's nan's terrier Mitzi has bitten two people, so she wears a muzzle when visitors come.» The clue is bitten. A muzzle here is a cover of straps or wire over a dog's nose and mouth, which stops it biting.
explain: «A broad glistening muzzle showed itself above the edge of the bank, and the Otter hauled himself out.» Nothing here is about a dog or a cover. The muzzle is the nose and mouth of an animal. Swap that meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A muzzle can be the nose and mouth of an animal, such as a dog or horse.
fact: A muzzle can also be a cover of straps or wire put over a dog's nose and mouth to stop it biting.
fact: The muzzle of a gun is the open end the bullet comes out of.
fact: To muzzle someone means to stop them speaking freely. Muzzle can be a noun or a verb.
exercise: «Kieran's nan's terrier Mitzi has bitten two people, so she wears a muzzle when visitors come.» What is a muzzle here? | A bowl for the dog's food | *A cover of straps or wire over a dog's nose and mouth | A loud bark that can be heard far away | A lead used for walking the dog
exercise: «A broad glistening muzzle showed itself above the edge of the bank, and the Otter hauled himself out.» What does muzzle mean here? | The open end of a gun | A tiny stone on the bank | *The nose and mouth of an animal | A soft towel
exercise: Dogs age faster than people, and an old dog may get grey fur round its muzzle. Find and copy the word that means the nose and mouth of an animal. | sleeps | fur | slowly | *muzzle
test: In the news, a government that stops newspapers from reporting freely is said to do what to the press? | Feed | Measure | *Muzzle | Wrap
test: Which part of a gun is the open end the bullet comes out of? | Sight | *Muzzle | Handle | Trigger
exam: In «she wears a muzzle when visitors come», what kind of word is muzzle? | *Noun | Verb | Adjective | Adverb
